@page "/how-it-works"
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

<PageTitle>How it works | BloodLink</PageTitle>
<PublicSite>
<main id="main-content" class="public-workflow">
    <section class="bl-container public-workflow-intro" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
        <div><span class="public-kicker">How BloodLink works</span><h1 id="workflow-title">From shortage to fulfilment, in one workflow.</h1><p class="public-lead">A clear sequence connects your facility's inventory, the people reviewing a need and the team responding to a request.</p><a class="public-text-link" href="/facility/register">Start with your facility <AppIcon Name="arrow-right" Size="18" /></a></div>
        <div class="public-workflow-map" role="img" aria-label="A blood need connects the requesting facility to availability across the network, then to a responding facility and confirmed handover">
            <div class="public-map-node"><AppIcon Name="building" Size="28" /><strong>Your facility</strong><span>Inventory + need</span></div>
            <div class="public-map-connection"><span>Review · Search · Request</span><AppIcon Name="arrow-right" Size="24" /></div>
            <div class="public-map-node public-map-network"><AppIcon Name="network" Size="36" /><strong>Facility network</strong><span>Availability + response</span></div>
            <div class="public-map-connection"><span>Accept · Handover</span><AppIcon Name="arrow-right" Size="24" /></div>
            <div class="public-map-node"><AppIcon Name="circle-check" Size="28" /><strong>Confirmed handover</strong><span>Updated records</span></div>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="public-timeline-section" aria-labelledby="sequence-title"><div class="bl-container">
        <div class="public-section-intro"><span class="public-kicker">The complete sequence</span><h2 id="sequence-title">Eight steps. A visible next action.</h2><p>Each stage has an owner, a decision and a record.</p></div>
        <ol class="public-timeline">
            <li><span class="public-stage-number">01</span><div><span class="public-kicker">Facility team</span><h3>Monitor inventory</h3><p>Review stock by blood type, including total, reserved and available units. Record adjustments as stock changes.</p></div><AppIcon Name="package" Size="30" /></li>
            <li><span class="public-stage-number">02</span><div><span class="public-kicker">Facility staff</span><h3>Record a blood need</h3><p>Submit the required blood type, units and supporting details so the facility administrator has the context to review.</p></div><AppIcon Name="clipboard-list" Size="30" /></li>
            <li><span class="public-stage-number">03</span><div><span class="public-kicker">Facility administrator</span><h3>Review the need</h3><p>Review the submitted need and determine the next action, including whether network coordination is needed.</p></div><AppIcon Name="eye" Size="30" /></li>
            <li><span class="public-stage-number">04</span><div><span class="public-kicker">Administrator + BloodLink</span><h3>Search availability</h3><p>The administrator starts an availability search. BloodLink presents matching stock across facilities for review.</p></div><AppIcon Name="search" Size="30" /></li>
            <li><span class="public-stage-number">05</span><div><span class="public-kicker">Requesting administrator</span><h3>Send a request</h3><p>Create a request to a facility with suitable availability. Follow it in requests sent and the associated need.</p></div><AppIcon Name="send" Size="30" /></li>
            <li><span class="public-stage-number">06</span><div><span class="public-kicker">Receiving administrator</span><h3>Respond to the request</h3><p>The receiving facility reviews the request, then accepts or rejects it. An accepted request reserves the agreed units.</p></div><AppIcon Name="inbox" Size="30" /></li>
            <li><span class="public-stage-number">07</span><div><span class="public-kicker">Receiving administrator</span><h3>Confirm the handover</h3><p>After the physical handover, confirm completion in BloodLink so the request moves to its completed state.</p></div><AppIcon Name="circle-check" Size="30" /></li>
            <li><span class="public-stage-number">08</span><div><span class="public-kicker">BloodLink records</span><h3>Update inventory and activity</h3><p>The completed workflow is reflected in stock transactions, request statuses and activity records for later review.</p></div><AppIcon Name="history" Size="30" /></li>
        </ol>
    </div></section>
    <section class="public-section bl-container" aria-labelledby="roles-title"><span class="public-kicker">Clear responsibilities</span><h2 id="roles-title">The right tools for each role.</h2><div class="public-role-grid"><article><AppIcon Name="user" Size="24" /><h3>Facility Staff</h3><p>View inventory, submit blood needs and follow their own needs.</p></article><article><AppIcon Name="building" Size="24" /><h3>Facility Admin</h3><p>Manage inventory, review needs, coordinate requests and maintain the facility team.</p></article><article><AppIcon Name="shield" Size="24" /><h3>System Admin</h3><p>Oversee facility access and governance across the network.</p></article></div></section>
    <section class="public-final-cta bl-container"><h2>Explore the tools behind every step.</h2><a class="bl-btn bl-btn-primary bl-btn-lg" href="/features">Explore features <AppIcon Name="arrow-right" Size="18" /></a></section>
</main>
</PublicSite>
